{
  "name": "Netskope Account Takeover — Detect, Enrich, Approve & Suspend",
  "description": "Runs every 15 minutes. Hunts three Netskope-native ATO signals confirmed present in this SDL tenant via live schema discovery on 2026-07-15: unmapped.alert_type == 'uba' (Netskope UBA anomaly), unmapped.alert_type == 'Compromised Credential', and unmapped.activity == 'Login Failed' bursts (>=5 per user in the 15m window). For each finding: enriches the source IP via VirusTotal, posts an Approve/Deny prompt to Slack, waits up to 30 minutes for an analyst response, and on approval suspends the user in Okta. On timeout or denial, logs a no-action message to the same Slack thread for manual follow-up. No S1-native alert exists for these Netskope findings in this tenant (detectionSource.product was null across all 950 sampled alert-source events), so this uses a Scheduled Trigger + PowerQuery hunt rather than a Singularity Response Trigger.",
